; JSON, shared. It was inside [writ_lsp] because the language server was the only
; thing that spoke it; [writ_mcp] speaks it too, and an MCP server that linked the
; whole language server to borrow a parser would be a dependency nobody could
; explain later.
;
; UNWRAPPED on purpose. Wrapped, these become [Writ_json.Json] and every existing
; [Json.] reference in the LSP tree would have to change or be aliased back —
; churn across a dozen files to rename a module that is already named exactly
; what it is. The cost is that [Json] and [Json_parse] are global module names;
; there are no others in this build, and a collision would be a compile error
; rather than a silent shadowing.

(library
 (name writ_json)
 (wrapped false))
